  "decision": {
    "r59_status": "PASS on the vendored curve for a single event, with >10x margin against even the 0402 floor; PASS on steady and average power. The one thing the curve cannot cover is the Q50 SOA during the same inrush, which is a different part.",
    "cut_delay_is_slower_than_rev_a": "at 15 V the gate crosses 13.5 V after 23.2 us, 1.7x the Rev A placeholder's 13.8 us, because 1008 pF is 17x the placeholder.  T2's 13.36 us input-delay energy must be re-read at this value; it stays negligible against the 1.28 mJ capacitor energy but the number moves.",
    "five_v_loss_does_not_kill_gate_drive_immediately": "the cut itself lands in ~23 us, but VDD_SR stays above the 3.63 V REG turn-off floor for milliseconds (3.95 V at +3 ms, 3.81 V at +6 ms) on the local 11.1 uF.  Below 4.13 V the UCC24624 can no longer hold REG in regulation, so the gate clamp is already out of spec.  The guarantee that the SR gates are off after a 5 V loss must come from a clamp in the 5 V domain, not from the bias cut.",
    "what_the_deck_cannot_close": "no Q50 SOA, no PCB thermal impedance, no CMOS output drive strength, no real DMP3098L model, no SR commutation."
  },
